body.p:
SVG
{EMBED HERE}
1.7534.283The third screen IM3-10 of the first display unit 450 does not include any information which indicates that information is displayed on the fourth screen IM4-10 that assists the occupant in driving in the manual mode. Absent identification of any disclosure in MIMURA relating to such feature, it is respectfully submitted that MIMURA may not be properly interpreted to disclose the above-mentioned features of amended independent claim 1. The Office Action even appears to acknowledge such deficiency of MIMURA. (See Office Action at page 9, lines 2-3).

SVG
{EMBED HERE}
1.652.30Accordingly, the auxiliary notification part in TAMURA emphasizes and notifies that the vehicle state notification information is displayed on the display unit, with the auxiliary notification part being displayed on such same display unit. In contrast, according to the features of amended independent claim 1, the third information indicates that the second information is displayed on a second display different from the first display on which the third information is displayed. Thus, even if the skilled artisan was to modify MIMURA to include an auxiliary notification part as taught by TAMURA to emphasize information displayed within a same display, Applicant respectfully submits that such resultant combination fails to arrive at the above- mentioned features of amended independent claim 1. As such, Applicant respectfully submits that TAMURA fails to cure the deficiencies of MIMURA.

SVG
{EMBED HERE}
